  (wire (pts (xy 436.88 160.02) (xy 436.88 157.48)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid 4466b45d-fda9-5717-961f-595c1e748290))
  (label "TVS_CHAIN_SPARE" (at 436.88 157.48 90) (fields_autoplaced) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 3ffd3c09-b779-5aa9-ac5b-d91f4b179096))
  (text "Both ribbons, end to end. J-CHAIN-MAIN-RH/-LH, the series resistors, R-SER-TERM, the beads and U-TVS-CHAIN are on the MAIN board; J-CHAIN-KEY-RH and J-CHAIN-KEY-LH are each\nkey board's J-CHAIN. CBL-CHAIN is not a part: a main-board pin and the key-board pin its conductor reaches are one net. Which board carries which part: key-chain-loom.md,\n'Which board places what'. Below: the nets that carry two ports - a register's QH is the next register's SER - and CHAIN_QH_RT, which reaches no connector." (at 25.4 25.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 0bb5c46e-e660-5426-b87f-bbc7063a854b))
  (text "FROM THE HAND-WRITTEN NETLIST THIS SHEET REPLACES (the part notes are on each part's Note field):\n\nAUTHORITATIVE for connectivity. The drawings on key-chain-loom.md are a REPRESENTATION of this file.\n\nTHE HOP MAP IS HERE, AS NETS. Chain order MCU <- RT <- RH <- LT <- LH (config/key-layout.yaml). right_thumb and left_thumb are on the main board; right_hand and left_hand are on the key boards, one\nIDC ribbon each. Each ribbon carries its key board's SER in on conductor 6 and its QH out on conductor 8, so every hop is a named net below.\n\nTHE REGISTER SIDE IS PER INSTANCE. cluster/key-register is one schematic built four times (`replicated: 4`) with generic CHAIN_SER / CHAIN_QH pins, so it cannot declare which instance sits on which\nhop. This file does, with one port per instance pin (CHAIN_SER_RT ... CHAIN_QH_LH), and hardware/nets.yaml marks those nets `per_board:` - the checker prints them rather than pretending the register\ndeclares them.\n\nTHE KEY-BOARD END NUMBERS THE CONDUCTORS DIFFERENTLY, AND THE CABLE SETS IT. Same 2x6 1.27 mm right-angle IDC header at both ends, the key board's mounted upside down on its underside, facing the same\nway. A keyed socket always mates position k to header pin k; CBL-CHAIN is ordered with its notch reversed on the key-board end (Samtec -RN2), so conductor k is main-board pin k and key-board pin 13-k\n[datasheet, both full prints banked; key-chain-loom.md].\n\nTHE CABLE IS NOT A COMPONENT HERE. CBL-CHAIN is a straight conductor per pin, so each ribbon is modelled as the nets it joins: a main-board pin and the key-board pin it reaches are on the same net.\n\nTHE CHAIN'S 3V3 IS DEV_3V3 ON THE MAIN BOARD, and each ribbon's conductor 10 is behind its own ferrite bead (ADR 0018). So V3V3_CHAIN - the name the replicated cluster schematics use - is the same\nnode as DEV_3V3 for the two registers on the main board, and each key board's rail is its own net past its bead (V3V3_CHAIN_RH, V3V3_CHAIN_LH), `per_board:` in hardware/nets.yaml like the hop nets.\nThere is no fuse: short-circuit protection is the Matrix LDO's own current limit (key-chain-loom.md).\n\n[CHAIN_SER_RT] one per register instance - see the header\n\n[CHAIN_SCK] One net each: right_thumb and left_thumb by trace, the key boards by ribbon.\n\n--- the hop map, from the chain end toward the MCU ------------------\n\n[CHAIN_SER_LH] Chain end: IO33 (or the pull-up) into left_hand's SER, over its ribbon.\n\n[HOP_LH_LT] left_hand's QH back over its ribbon into left_thumb's SER.\n\n[HOP_LT_RH] left_thumb's QH out over the right_hand ribbon into right_hand's SER.\n\n[HOP_RH_RT] right_hand's QH back over its ribbon into right_thumb's SER.\n\n[CHAIN_QH_RT] ONE NET, TWO BOUNDARIES: right_thumb's QH is a main-board trace to the MCU's pin. It reaches no connector, so the TVS is not on it.\n\n[DEV_3V3] ONE NET, TWO BOUNDARIES: the Matrix's 3V3 arriving from carrier/carrier, and the chain rail the main-board registers and R-SER-TERM sit on.\n\n[V3V3_CHAIN_RH] Each key board's rail, past its ribbon's bead.\n\n[CHAIN_SPARE_RH_11] ADR 0009's rule: two spare conductors per ribbon, end to end, unallocated." (at 25.4 279.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid be950bfb-8199-5567-a48e-d9f2f1b4c8b7))
